  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 2(b): the same initial blueprint after the automated prover's sorry-filling pass. Rectangles are definitions and ellipses are theorems; dashed arrows mark a statement-level use and solid arrows a proof-level use. Definition nodes taylorKernel, taylorRemainderKernel, taylorPoly, lineMap and lineCurve sit at the top; the target frechet_taylor_integral is the sink at the bottom. The leaf lemmas taylorKernel_deriv_t, taylorKernel_at_right and taylorRemainder_eq_explicit have turned dark green; taylor_integral_kernel and lineCurve_iteratedDeriv remain light blue, and taylor_integral_explicit and frechet_taylor_integral are filled a lighter green; the caption distinguishes only blue (unproved) from green (proved), so what the two shades of green separate is not stated in the paper.",
